
==============================================================================
19.1 Which is a uniform plane TEM wave (multiple choice)
==============================================================================
  (a) E=z f(t-z/c), H=x f/eta0               Faraday 1.0e+00  Ampere 1.4e+00  divE/|curlE| 1.2e+30  -> FAILS
  (b) E=y f(t-z/c), H=+x f/eta0              Faraday 2.0e+00  Ampere 2.0e+00  divE/|curlE| 0.0e+00  -> FAILS
  (c) E=z f(t+x/c), H=+y f/eta0              Faraday 3.7e-08  Ampere 3.7e-08  divE/|curlE| 0.0e+00  -> satisfies Maxwell
  (d) E=x e^-(y/a)^2 f(t-z/c), H=y ...       Faraday 7.1e-01  Ampere 2.5e-08  divE/|curlE| 0.0e+00  -> FAILS
  (e) E=x f(t-z/c), H=y f/(2 eta0)           Faraday 5.0e-01  Ampere 5.0e-01  divE/|curlE| 0.0e+00  -> FAILS
  (b) E x H direction: -z  but travel +z
  (c) E x H direction: -x  travel -x (t + x/c);  u x E = (-x) x z = +y
  (a) E along z, travel along z: div E = dEz/dz != 0 -> not TEM

==============================================================================
19.2 Sheet on y = 0 with Js = +z g(t), free space
==============================================================================
  y>0: n=+y, Js x n: z x y = -x -> H = -1/2 g x_hat
  y<0: n=-y, z x (-y) = +x -> H = +1/2 g x_hat
  eta0/2 * 0.5 = 94.25 V/m (60pi*0.5 = 30pi = 94.25); exact eta0: 94.18
  y=+150 m, t=1 us: delay 0.50 us, source time +0.50 us, g = 0.5 -> E = [ -0.          -0.         -94.24777961] V/m, H = [-0.25  0.    0.  ] A/m
  y=-450 m, t=1 us: delay 1.50 us, source time -0.50 us, g = 0.0 -> E = [-0. -0. -0.] V/m, H = [0. 0. 0.] A/m
  [19.2 fields] Faraday rel.res 6.4e-07 | Ampere-Maxwell 6.4e-07 | div/curl 0.0e+00 -> OK
  [19.2] at the sheet: E_t continuous and n x (H1 - H2) = Js -> OK
  jump check with g=0.5: y x (H+ - H-) = [0.  0.  0.5] = +0.5 z ✓
  S direction y>0: (-z) x (-x) = +y ; y<0: (-z) x (+x) = -y
  static (Lecture 13) sheet 0.5 A/m: H = 1/2 Js x n =  [-0.25  0.    0.  ] above (same as radiated, undelayed)

==============================================================================
19.3 True or false (sheet facts)
==============================================================================
  (a) E just above = E just below: T (E even); (b) H equal: F (H reverses, jump = Js)
  (c) plane wave does not decay with distance: amplitude independent of d -> F
  (d) Js.E = -(eta/2)|Js|^2 < 0 -> T; e.g. Js=1 A/m: Js.E = -188.3651567821601 W/m^2
  (e) er=1: E amp per 1 A/m = 188.4 V/m, H amp = 0.5 A/m, v = 2.9979e+08
  (e) er=4: E amp per 1 A/m = 94.2 V/m, H amp = 0.5 A/m, v = 1.4990e+08
  (e) ratio E(er=4)/E(er=1) = 0.5  -> T
  (f) z<0 side of sheet on z=0 (Js = x f): E x H = (-x) x (+y) = -z  -> 'along +z' is F

==============================================================================
19.4 Reading wave parameters: H = 0.05 cos(6pi e8 t - 4 pi z) x_hat A/m
==============================================================================
  omega = 1.8850e+09 rad/s, f = 3.0000e+08 Hz, beta = 12.5664 rad/m, lambda = 0.5000 m
  v_p = 1.5000e+08 m/s, er = (c/v)^2 = 4.0000 (course c) / 3.9945 (exact c)
  eta = mu0 v_p = 188.4956 Ohm (= 60 pi = 188.4956); eta0/2 = 188.37
  E amplitude = eta*0.05 = 9.4248 V/m (3 pi = 9.4248)
  E = eta H x u: x x z = -y -> E = -y 9.42 cos(...)
  check E x H: (-y) x x = +z  = travel +z ✓
  [19.4 fields (mu0, eps = mu0^-1 v^-2)] Faraday rel.res 3.3e-09 | Ampere-Maxwell 3.3e-09 | div/curl 0.0e+00 -> OK

==============================================================================
19.5 Find the error: sheet on x = 0, Js = -y g(t)
==============================================================================
  correct x>0: (-y) x (+x) = +z -> H = +1/2 g z
  correct x<0: (-y) x (-x) = -z -> H = -1/2 g z
  E = -(eta0/2)(-y) g = +(eta0/2) g y on both sides
  student x<0: H = +1/2 g z, E = eta0 H x u, u=-x: z x (-x) = -y -> student E = -(eta0/2) g y (wrong)
  student x>0: z x x = +y -> +(eta0/2) g y (accidentally right)
  [19.5 correct fields] Faraday rel.res 1.9e-06 | Ampere-Maxwell 1.9e-06 | div/curl 0.0e+00 -> OK
  [19.5 correct] at the sheet: E_t continuous and n x (H1 - H2) = Js -> OK
  student jump x(H+ - H-) = [0. 0. 0.]  vs Js = [-0. -1. -0.]  -> student violates the H jump
  student E jump: E(0+) - E(0-) = [  0.   376.73   0.  ]  (= eta0 g y) -> violates E_t continuity
  S check correct x<0: (+y) x (-z) = -x (away ✓)
  E vs Js: E along +y, Js along -y -> opposite ✓

